-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",101,{
[3201]="70018F0D\n1\tDefeat Globsnaga warriors within Buzun-ghâr (total: 4)\030Execute Nimpheleg's plan to destroy the source of the wilting rot\030Defeat Globsnaga skirmishers within Buzun-ghâr (total: 3)\tNimpheleg is at Lossathrod, the camp-site within Buzun-ghâr, located off Durin's Way. Globsnaga Orcs can be found throughout Buzun-ghâr. Since Orvar has refused to seal the newly-excavated passage, Corunothiel has asked you to work with her friend Nimpheleg to locate and destroy the source of the wilting rot within Buzun-ghâr, and to defeat the Globsnaga that have been affected by or drawn to the corruption.\n2\tTalk to Corunothiel\tCorunothiel is at Lossathrod, the encampment of Elves and dwarves at the top of Buzun-ghâr. You have dealt with the wilting rot within Buzun-ghâr and should speak now to Corunothiel of your successes.\n3\tTalk to Orvar\tOrvar Bellhammer is at Lossathrod, the encampment within the passage of Buzun-ghâr, located off of Durin's Way. Corunothiel said that a message for you was delivered to Orvar while you were in the depths of Buzun-ghâr, and you should speak to the dwarf to learn its content.\n",
[3202]="7001A97C\n1\tTalk to Otri Greyhammer in the Haunted Inn\tOtri Greyhammer is inside the Haunted Inn. Cúcheron told you to speak with Otri Greyhammer about some problem that has plagued the dwarves.\n2\tFind Rósar Greyhammer and ensure his safety\030Find Stígur Greyhammer and ensure his safety\tRósar and Stígur Greyhammer are lost somewhere within the fens of the Drownholt, south of the Dourstocks. Otri Greyhammer is desperate for you to find his brothers, lost within the marshes of the Drownholt.\n3\tTalk to Otri Greyhammer in the Haunted Inn\tOtri Greyhammer is by the fireplace in the Haunted Inn, among the Dourstocks. You have broken the Greyhammer brothers from their reveries and should return now to Otri.\n4\tTalk to Bróin in the cellar of the Haunted Inn\tBróin is in the cellar of the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks. Otri has asked you to tell Bróin that his brothers are safe and to see if the Hidden Guard has yet decided on a route.\n",
[3203]="7001424F\n1\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bósi is worried by what he has read of Balin's fate in the Book of Mazarbul, and wants you to warn his cousin to be more cautious.\n",
[3204]="700599FE\n1\tFind Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave, south-west of the Steepset\tEskil Bloodthumb is at the entrance to Deepscrave from Máttugard, south-west of the Steepset.\n2\tTalk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave\tStáli the Hewer's assistant, Eskil Bloodthumb, stands at the entrance to Deepscrave.\n3\tObserve Eskil's fighting form\tEskil Bloodthumb has asked you to observe his fighting style so you can give him pointers about his combat form.\n4\tPick up Eskil's fumbled axe\tEskil has dropped his axe, fumbling it while trying to show off his fighting form for you.\n5\tGive Eskil back his axe\tEskil Bloodthumb stands at the entrance to Deepscrave, weaponless and ashamed of his clumsiness.\n6\tWorried that he lacks the necessary training to successfully investigate Deepscrave, Eskil Bloodthumb has asked you to find a teacher at Maergrind willing to help him hone his skills.\t\n7\tTalk to Eskil Bloodthumb at the entrance to Deepscrave\tEskil Bloodthumb is still at the entrance to Deepscrave, waiting for the news that you found him a teacher.\n8\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind, the Noble Gate\tStáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.\n",
[3205]="7004CF37\n1\tJourney to the entrance of Felegoth in the north-eastern reaches of Eryn Lasgalen\tFelegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, can be found in the north-eastern woods of Eryn Lasgalen. The steed near King Thranduil outside the ruins of Dol Guldur can take you to Eryn Lasgalen with utmost speed.\n2\tTalk to Limlang at the entrance to Felegoth\tYou have come to Felegoth, the Halls of the Elvenking, and should make yourself known to Limlang, the guard at the entrance.\n3\tTalk to King Thranduil at his throne in Felegoth\tKing Thranduil is at his throne in the north-eastern chamber of Felegoth.\n4\tTalk to Legolas in the throne room of Felegoth\tLegolas has come to his father's throne room in Felegoth.\n5\tTalk to Gondil in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room\030Talk to Herthír in the dining chamber east of the throne room\030Talk to Itheron on the river-bridge, east of the throne room\tLegolas invited you to visit the dining chamber, the Room of Study, and the water-way bridge in Felegoth, and to speak to the Elves you find at those locations.\n6\tTalk to Legolas in the throne room of Felegoth\tLegolas is in his father's throne room, in Felegoth.\n",
[3206]="70067348\n1\tEnter the settlement of Jax Phanâl\tThe settlement of Jax Phanâl is to the east.\n2\tTalk to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl\tJâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.\n3\tDriftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.\t\n4\tTalk to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl\tJâkin is in the settlement of Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.\n5\tDefeat Haradrim at Grijâti south of Jax Phanâl (total: 8)\030Retrieve Umbari Book of History\030Retrieve Umbari Book of Romance\030Retrieve Umbari Book of Flora\tThe Haradrim that were pushed out of Jax Phanâl have a camp to the south where they keep the things they stole.\n6\tBring the stolen books back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl\tYou recovered the stolen books and should bring them back to Jâkin in Jax Phanâl.\n7\tDriftwood has accompanied you to Jax Phanâl, on the Cape of Umbar.\t\n8\tTalk to Nauriel outside Jax Phanâl\tNauriel has made the crossing from the Shield Isles to the Cape of Umbar, and you should speak with her outside Jax Phanâl.\n",
[3207]="70059A00\n1\tStáli the Hewer has presented you with a contract requiring you to assist him. It is your choice whether to sign the document or tell him no.\t\n2\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind\tStáli the Hewer is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate.\n3\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard\tDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\n4\tDefeat Orcs or goblins in Deepscrave (total: 12)\030Search debris at the lower extent of the Berg-beam\030Search debris near the midpoint of the Berg-beam\030Search debris at the upper extent of the Berg-beam\tDurin asked you to examine the Berg-beam in Deepscrave for signs of weakness and to combat any Orcs you find there. While you are on the prince's business, you may as well keep your eyes open for the jewels sought by Stáli the Hewer.\n5\tBring the rusted dagger and dirty gem to Stáli the Hewer at Maergrind in Máttugard\tStáli the Hewer is waiting for you to emerge from Deepscrave and bring him the fruits of your search. He is at Maergrind in Máttugard.\n",
[3208]="7004CF63\n1\tTalk to Gardelen\tThranduil's scouts Gardelen and Dínellas patrol the wood south-east of Torech Emel.\n2\tDefeat foes in Eryn Lasgalen (total: 8)\tFoes of the Elves have been stirred up by the passage of Orcs through Eryn Lasgalen, and Gardelen has asked you to defeat them if you can.\n3\tDínellas followed a band of Orc-spies through Eryn Lasgalen. Gardelen believed the Orcs were bound for Caras Tilion, and you should seek the hunter Dínellas by the old Elf-hall there.\t\n4\tSearch the Orc-spy slain by Dínellas\tThe Orc-spy slain by Dínellas can be found by his position near Caras Tilion.\n5\tShow the letter for Karazgar to Dínellas near Caras Tilion\tDínellas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.\n6\tShow the letter for Karazgar to Legolas near Caras Tilion\tLegolas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.\n7\tDefeat foes within Caras Tilion (total: 10)\tLegolas asked you to defeat foes within his old home of Caras Tilion while he considers the meaning of the letter you discovered.\n8\tTalk to Legolas near Caras Tilion\tLegolas is near the ruins of the Elf-hall at Caras Tilion.\n9\tTalk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth\tThranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.\n",
[3209]="70067349\n1\tTravel south along the coast to Rakhatâb\tRakhatâb is located on the southern promontory of the Cape of Umbar.\n2\tTalk to the woman in the crowd\tA crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.\n3\tTalk to the man in the crowd\tA crowd gathers around a body on the ground in Rakhatâb.\n4\tExamine the body of the victim\tThe body of an aged man lies dead on the ground in Rakhatâb.\n5\tTalk to the guard in Rakhatâb\tA guard has called for you to step away from the body, and glares at you with distrust.\n6\tTalk to Daxamat by the crowd in Rakhatâb\tDaxamat stands by the crowd in Rakhatâb.\n7\tDefeat Corsairs in the Cape of Umbar and at Kan Skûrja, north-east of Rakhatâb (total: 10)\tFolk in the crowd believe one of the Corsairs from the camp to the north-east, up the coastline, may be responsible for the brazen murder in Rakhatâb.\n8\tTalk to Daxamat outside Rakhatâb\tDaxamat is outside Rakhatâb, waiting to hear what you learned from the Corsairs.\n9\tWait for Daxamat to run off\tDaxamat runs off to distract the guards.\n10\tSearch the evidence coffer outside the keep in Rakhatâb\tThe coffer containing evidence taken from the victim of the murder in Rakhatâb is outside the keep, to the south-east.\n11\tMeet up with your crew on the beach to the south-east of Rakhatâb\tYou agreed to meet with your crew outside Rakhatâb on the south-eastern beach to examine the evidence you retrieved.\n12\tTalk to Sirgon outside Rakhatâb\tSirgon is at your meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.\n13\tShow the evidence you recovered to Daxamat south-east of Rakhatâb\tDaxamat has arrived at your meeting spot south-east of Rakhatâb, and you should show him the evidence you retrieved from the coffer.\n",
[3210]="7006734A\n1\tDriftwood is outside Rakhatâb.\t\n2\tTalk to Caebar outside Rakhatâb\tCaebar is at the meeting spot outside Rakhatâb.\n3\tTravel to the village of Khûtra, north-east of Rakhatâb\tThe village of Khûtra is north-east of Rakhatâb along the coast road that runs to the City of the Corsairs.\n4\tTalk to Bôdo in Khûtra\tBôdo is unsure what to make of your arrival to his village.\n5\tCollect driftwood along the beach (total: 6)\030Collect crab legs (total: 6)\tYou were asked to collect things that may help Khûtra survive the famine with which it has been gripped in recent days.\n6\tBring the driftwood and crab legs to Bôdo in the village of Khûtra\tBôdo waits for you to return to him in the village of Khûtra.\n7\tFind the woman Bôdo described atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra\tBôdo told you a woman was looking for you, and could be found atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.\n8\tTalk to the woman north-east of Khûtra\tA woman has asked to speak with you atop the rocks north-east of Khûtra.\n9\tRemain alert\tCruel Dancer moves swiftly, and then she is gone.\n10\tTalk to Gimli north-east of the village of Khûtra\tGimli waits for you north-east of the village of Khûtra.\n",
[3211]="7004CF8F\n1\tFind Mithrandir and the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room\tMithrandir is meeting with the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room\tMithrandir is meeting with the scholars of Felegoth in the Room of Study, south-east of the throne room.\n3\tReturn to Thranduil in the throne room of Felegoth\tMithrandir asked you to inquire of Thranduil if the Bugdatish might have been part of Smaug's treasure-hoard.\n4\tTalk to Thranduil in his throne room in Felegoth\tThranduil is in his throne room in Felegoth.\n5\tTalk to Mithrandir in the throne room of Felegoth\tMithrandir is in the throne room of Felegoth.\n6\tTravel to Loeglond and seek tidings of Karazgar or the Bugdatish\tLoeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, is in the Dale-lands along the river. Mithrandir suggested that you visit the Raft-elves on your way to Erebor, seeking news of Karazgar and the Bugdatish.\n7\tTalk to Nembadeth at Loeglond\tLoeglond, the settlement of the Raft-elves, is in the Dale-lands along the river. Mithrandir suggested that you visit the Raft-elves on your way to Erebor, seeking news of Karazgar and the Bugdatish.\n",
[3212]="700599FF\n1\tTalk to Durin at Maergrind in Máttugard\tDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard.\n2\tSearch the mess of assorted papers at a camp-fire inside Durshulot\030Recover a record of the takeover from Orcs guarding the north-western approach to Durshulot\030Recover a litany of complaints from Orcs guarding the north-eastern approach to Durshulot\tDurin has asked you to search Durshulot in Deepscrave to learn what you can about Gorgar the Ruthless and his rule of the Orcs.\n3\tBring the readable pages you recovered from Deepscrave to Durin at Maergrind\tDurin is at Maergrind, the Noble Gate, in Máttugard. You have recovered a number of readable documents that may shed light on Gorgar's rule of the Orcs within Gundabad, and should bring them to Prince Durin for his study.\n4\tTalk to Trausti at Maergrind in Máttugard\tTrausti has suddenly arrived and called for your attention. What has happened?\n",
[3213]="700599FD\n1\tMeet up with Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave\tTrausti has urged you to meet him in Deepscrave on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in sight of where he lost Eskil Bloodthumb.\n2\tTalk to Trausti on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, in Deepscrave\tTrausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam in Deepscrave, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.\n3\tSearch the site of the attack for clues to Eskil's fate\tThe site of the attack is to the north-west of Trausti's location.\n4\tThe site of the attack is in Deepscrave, north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?\t\n5\tThe site of the attack is north-west of Trausti's location. What clues might it hold for Eskil's fate?\t\n6\tTalk to Trausti at the Berg-beam in Deepscrave\tTrausti is on the north-western side of the Berg-beam, near the site where Eskil Bloodthumb was left behind.\n7\tSearch for Eskil Bloodthumb north-east of Durshulot, among dwellings along the outer wall of Deepscrave\tTrausti believes Eskil may have been brought through the Orc-village of Durshulot, perhaps to dwellings along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave.\n8\tTalk to Trausti in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave\tTrausti is in a ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, searching for Eskil Bloodthumb.\n9\tLet loose a mighty roar!\tTrausti thinks someone is lurking in the ramshackle dwelling, and if you roar you may be able to frighten him from his hiding-place.\n10\tTalk to the frightened goblin\tA frightened goblin cowers in the ramshackle dwelling. Does he know anything about Eskil's fate?\n11\tThe goblin is frightened!\tThe frightened goblin makes good his escape!\n12\tTalk to Trausti in the ramshackle dwelling on the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave\tTrausti is in the ramshackle dwelling along the north-eastern wall of Deepscrave, musing over what you have learned.\n",
[3214]="7004CFD0\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Lake-town\tLake-town is to the north-east of Loeglond. Nembadeth sent you to speak with Várthrek, a guard at the entrance to Lake-town.\n2\tTalk to Várthrek at the entrance to Lake-town\tLake-town is to the north-east of Loeglond. Nembadeth sent you to speak with Várthrek, a guard at the entrance to Lake-town.\n3\tAsk around Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar\tVárthrek told you to ask the townsfolk of Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar.\n4\tAsk around Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar\tVárthrek told you to ask the townsfolk of Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar.\n5\tAsk around Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar\tVárthrek told you to ask the townsfolk of Lake-town for tidings of Karazgar.\n6\tTalk to Kólfith on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water\tKólfith is on the lower level of Lake-town, just above the water.\n7\tTalk to Fasti outside the Dragonbone Inn and meet with Kólfith in secret\tKólfith wants to meet you inside the Dragonbone Inn, in the northern section of Lake-town. He asked you to speak with Fasti outside the inn to arrange a safe meeting.\n8\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter just north of the Dragonbone Inn\tAuthi, the dwarf you befriended in the Dragonbone Inn, is just to the north of the tavern.\n",
[3215]="7006734B\n1\tDefeat the Dead outside the ruined temple of Sauron (total: 8)\tThe Dead that linger near the ruined temple of Sauron to the east will endanger any who travel to the City of the Corsairs.\n2\tTalk to Sirgon outside the ruined temple of Sauron\tSirgon has come as near to the ruined temple of Sauron as he wishes.\n3\tTravel south-west where you can have a view of the Calatirion's wreckage\tThe wreckage of Calatirion on the hill of Kharn Arâx can be found to the south-west.\n4\tTalk to Legolas in view of the wreckage of Calatirion\tLegolas looks up at the wreckage of Calatirion, musing about what he has been told of its history.\n5\tMeet up with your crew further ahead, beside the road to Umbar Baharbêl\tYour crew plans to meet on the road to Umbar Baharbêl, and you should join them.\n6\tTalk to Daxamat by the road to Umbar Baharbêl\tDaxamat stands by the road to Umbar Baharbêl with the rest of your crew.\n",
[3216]="7004CFF2\n1\tDefeat beasts on the way to the Lonely Mountain (total: 10)\tAuthi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He asked you to defeat troublesome beasts on the way to the Lonely Mountain.\n2\tTravel to the Lonely Mountain, north of Dale, and meet with Authi\tAuthi Gem-cutter invited you to go to Erebor to consult with King Thorin about the mysterious decline in the craft-skill of the dwarves. He said he would meet you at the Lonely Mountain.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf at the Lonely Mountain\tGandalf has come to Erebor, and he stands outside the entrance to the Hall Under the Mountain.\n4\tFind the visitors Gandalf mentioned on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain\tGandalf hinted that some old friends could be found on the way to the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n5\tTalk to Dwalin\030Talk to Glóin\030Talk to Dori\tAs Gandalf hinted, a number of Thorin Oakenshield's companions have come to Erebor. What has drawn them here?\n6\tTalk to Gandalf in the Hall Under the Mountain\tGandalf is in the Hall Under the Mountain near several dwarves of Thorin's Company who have come to Erebor.\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain\tKing Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n",
[3217]="70059A03\n1\tMeet up with Trausti by the base of the Berg-beam\tTrausti has suggested that you meet with him at the base of the Berg-beam, at the lowest level of Deepscrave.\n2\tTalk to Trausti near the base of the Berg-beam\tTrausti is at the base of the Berg-beam, preparing for the rescue of Eskil Bloodthumb.\n3\tTalk to Trausti and attempt to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb\tTrausti is near the base of the Berg-beam, ready to rescue Eskil Bloodthumb.\n4\tTalk to Eskil Bloodthumb at Maergrind in Máttugard\tYou have rescued Eskil Bloodthumb and returned him safely to Maergrind in Máttugard, where he waits to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Fastrith Hawkfeast at Maergrind in Máttugard\tEskil's sister Fastrith Hawkfeast has asked to speak to you.\n",
[3218]="7006734C\n1\tWait for your crew to disperse\tThe crew separates and prepares to enter the city by different paths.\n2\tEnter Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate, which leads to the Sail-haven\tYou will enter the city by the Beacon Gate, which provides entrance to the north-western area of the city.\n3\tTalk to Caebar by the Beacon Gate\tCaebar has entered Umbar Baharbêl by the Beacon Gate on the north-western side of the city.\n4\tComplete 'The City: The Eyes of Nauriel'\030Complete 'The City: Sirgon's Wound'\030Complete 'The City: Sigileth's Curiosity'\030Complete 'The City: Elves, Dwarves, and Trouble'\030Complete 'The City: The Short Straw'\tYour crew has split up to search Umbar Baharbêl for information that will aid in the rescue of Thorongil and the completion of your mission.\n5\tTalk to Caebar at a market in the Sail-haven\tCaebar said he would meet you at one of the markets in the Sail-haven when you have learned what your crew discovered.\n",
[3219]="70067CB6\n1\tRead the note Caebar discovered on his person\tCaebar handed you the note he discovered in his pocket, and you should read it.\n2\tTalk to Caebar in the Sail-haven\tCaebar is in the Sail-haven.\n3\tFind the camp of crocodiles to the south-east of the city\tCruel Dancer spoke of crocodiles outside the city, and Caebar believes she means the ones that can be found to the south-east.\n4\tFind the lamp nearest the crocodiles, on the rocks to the west\tCruel Dancer spoke of lamps in the night, somewhere near the crocodiles.\n5\tExamine the toppled lamp\tThe toppled lamp to the west of the crocodiles merits some examination.\n6\tExamine another toppled lamp to the west along the rocks\tAnother lamp lies to the west.\n7\tConfront the person watching you to the west of the line of lamps\tSomeone watches you from the rocks to the west of the line of lamps.\n8\tTalk to Cruel Dancer by the coil of rope\tCruel Dancer is west of the line of lamps, standing upon the rocks overlooking the river.\n",
[3220]="70059A02\n1\tStáli the Hewer's luggage can be found upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn.\t\n2\tYou hear footsteps approaching\tYou hear footsteps approaching.\n3\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer upstairs in Zarkul-sulûn\tStáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn.\n4\tExamine Eskil's contract\tStáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.\n5\tExamine Eskil's contract\tStáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.\n6\tExamine Eskil's contract\tStáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.\n7\tExamine Eskil's contract\tStáli the Hewer has returned to Zarkul-sulûn, and he holds Eskil's contract out for your study.\n8\tTalk to Eskil Bloodthumb in Zarkul-sulûn\tEskil Bloodthumb stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, looking resigned to his fate.\n9\tTalk to Fastrith Hawkfeast in Zarkul-sulûn\tFastrith Hawkfeast stands on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn, seeking to gain your attention.\n10\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer in Zarkul-sulûn\tStáli the Hewer is on the upper level of Zarkul-sulûn.\n11\tTalk to Durin on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn\tPrince Durin is on the lower level of Zarkul-sulûn.\n",
[3221]="7004D01A\n1\tTalk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain\tGandalf wishes to speak with you by the throne of King Thorin III, in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n2\tFind Dís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, at Raven-hill\tDís is at Raven-hill, south-west of the Lonely Mountain.\n3\tTalk to Dís at Raven-hill\tDís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.\n4\tClear brush from the path up Raven-hill (total: 6)\030Clear stones from the path up Raven-hill (total: 4)\tYou offered to clear the brush and stones from the path up Raven-hill for Dís.\n5\tTalk to Dís at Raven-hill\tDís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.\n6\tPick up the bucket of water at the base of Raven-hill\tYou volunteered to bring water from the well at the base of Raven-hill to Dís.\n7\tTalk to Dís at Raven-hill\tDís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.\n8\tDefeat foes near Dale for Dís (total: 10)\tYou volunteered to defeat foes in the vicinity of Dale for Dís.\n9\tTalk to Dís at Raven-hill\tDís, the sister of Thorin Oakenshield, is at Raven-hill.\n",
[3222]="70067CB7\n1\tUse the coil of rope and climb down to the secret grotto\tThe coil of rope by Cruel Dancer will allow you to reach the lair Cruel Dancer discovered.\n2\tTalk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city\tYou rescued one prisoner from the Kindred of the Coins, and your friends now recover at the amphitheatre east of the city.\n",
[3223]="7004D021\n1\tTalk to Gandalf at Raven-hill and travel to Mazal Akrâz\tGandalf is at Raven-hill, waiting to travel with you and the surviving members of Thorin's Company to ensure the Arkenstone remains entombed with the Oakenshield.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain\tKing Thorin III is at his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain\tGandalf is by the throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\n",
[3224]="70067CBA\n1\tWait for Driftwood to arrive\tCorudan looks around eagerly.\n2\tTalk to Driftwood at the amphitheatre east of the city\tDriftwood greets Corudan warmly.\n3\tTalk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city\tCorudan is pleased to see his friends again.\n4\tAn awkward silence fills the air\tDriftwood remains silent.\n5\tTalk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city\tCorudan looks at you carefully.\n6\tTalk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city\tSigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.\n",
[3225]="70067CBB\n1\tThink about what to tell Corudan\tCorudan is eager to hear what befell his friends... but you do not know how to tell him some of the mournful things that transpired.\n2\tTalk to Corudan at the amphitheatre east of the city\tCorudan waits for you to speak.\n3\tTalk to Sigileth at the amphitheatre east of the city\tSigileth is at the amphitheatre east of the city.\n",
[3226]="70049630\n1\tAsk Galadriel for the gift\tYou should ask Lady Galadriel in the Court of Lothlórien for Arwen's gift.\n2\tDeliver the gift to Arwen in Imlad Gelair\tGift in hand, it is time to visit Arwen in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell, once more.\n3\tWalk with Arwen to the bridge\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Go with Arwen to the bridge ahead.\n4\tTalk to Arwen\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Talk to Arwen upon the bridge.\n5\tWalk with Arwen to the left statue\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Go with Arwen to the left past the bridge, where the statue stands.\n6\tTalk to Arwen\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Talk to Arwen by the statue.\n7\tWalk with Arwen some more\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Go with Arwen farther down the path, through the narrow pass.\n8\tTalk to Arwen\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Talk to Arwen under the trees before the second bridge.\n9\tWalk with Arwen a little further\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Go with Arwen onto the second bridge.\n10\tTalk to Arwen\tArwen has asked you to walk with her in Imlad Gelair in Rivendell. If you get separated, ring the bell. Talk to Arwen upon the second bridge.\n",
[3227]="700143D9\n1\tCollect Dented Armour (total: 10)\030Collect Broken Blade (total: 10)\030Collect Cracked Shield (total: 10)\tDented armour, broken blades, and cracked shields can be found on Orcs and within their camps throughout Zelem-melek and the Redhorn Lodes. Bori needs to equip the two teams that will execute his strike on Stazgnâkh, and wants you to gather the materials that will allow him to do this.\n2\tBring armour, blades, and shields to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. You have collected many pieces of the equipment for which Bori has asked, and should now bring them to him.\n",
[3228]="70014646\n1\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. Brogur has told you that his nephew Bori wants to speak with you about something.\n2\tMemorize room plaques (total: 5)\tRoom plaques can be found throughout the Water-works, as well as dangerous aquatic creatures. Bori has asked you to memorize the locations of plaques in several different rooms throughout the Water-works.\n3\tDefeat creatures in the Water-works (total: 12)\tDangerous aquatic creatues can be found throughout the Water-works. Bori has asked you to defeat creatures located amongst the ruins of the Water-works.\n4\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. You have scouted the Water-works for sign of the armouries the dwarf Óin sought, as recorded in the Book of Mazarbul, and should return now to Bori.\n",
[3229]="7000F0F9\n1\tTalk to Brogur\tBósi's cousin Brogur is somewhere along the road that winds up to the Hollin Gate, north of Bósi's position. Bósi has asked you to lend your aid to his cousin Brogur while the pick-axes are being crafted.\n",
[3230]="70014250\n1\tTalk to Sebbi\030Talk to Wethur\030Talk to Stilling\030Talk to Sigthorn\030Talk to Wíli\030Talk to Skygni\tThe Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek is full of dwarves that Bori wants to recruit for his daring mission against the White Hand. Bori needs to fill two groups with dwarves: a diversionary force and a main attack group.\n2\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have attempted to recruit some dwarves for Bori's daring plan to drive the White Hand from Moria, but very few of the dwarves have volunteered.\n",
[3231]="700147EC\n1\tPlace Elf-stones at abyss cracks (total: 3)\030Collect Bag of Beryls\tCracks in the abyss can be found throughout the Foundations of Stone, not far from Gwathrendath. Lenglammel has asked you to place Elf-stones in front of abyss-cracks near the camp to dissuade nameless creatures from approaching.\n2\tTalk to Lenglammel\tLenglammel is in the camp of Gwathrendath, among the Foundations of Stone. You have done what you can to counter the threat of the nameless creatures that lurk among the Foundations of Stone.\n",
[3232]="7002099A\n1\tTalk to Calenglad at Tinnudir\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim. Daervunn has sent you to enlist the aid of Calenglad and the Rangers of Evendim for the Grey Company.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad and travel with him to the Flooded Ward\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim. Calenglad is waiting to speak with you about taking one more journey into Annúminas to rescue some relics from the Angmarim and tomb-robbers that seek to plunder them.\n3\tTalk to Calenglad at Tinnudir\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, the Ranger-camp on the shores of Lake Evendim. You have done as Calenglad asked, and in his own way, he has bade farewell to the lands of Evendim. He is ready now to travel with the Grey Company, and you should speak with him.\n",
})
